Here is an example of some code which shows how to implement Mac OS 8 (Tempo) adornments in a grid view.  The technique being proposed is to implement an adorner for both a main grid view and a columns grid view.  The main grid view is subclassed to perform row selections (see the Row Select example for details) and the columns grid view is subclassed to perform column selections and to do special highlighting of its selection.When the columns view changes its selection, the main view's adorner is notified so that it updates the hilited column.